{"ts": 0.159477, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule\u001b[0m \u001b[90m----------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m \u001b[93menv  4/6\u001b[0m \u001b[90m--\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 127}
{"ts": 0.159527, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.159582, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mThe prompt is a variable\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThe text before your cursor is the variable \u001b[92mPS1\u001b[0m. Change it and the\r\nprompt changes at once.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mPS1='me> '\u001b[0m        \u001b[90m# the prompt is now me>\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 206}
{"ts": 0.159603, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "  \u001b[92mPS1='$ '\u001b[0m          \u001b[90m# and now a plain dollar sign\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThat last one is the prompt most terminals show. Watch the next\r\nscreen: the prompt will be back to shelltutor>.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m> Change it twice, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 244}
{"ts": 0.1635, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
{"ts": 0.16374, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 91}
